      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="154" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ we cwædon be ðam anfealdum ordale æt þam monnum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.10"/> þe oft betihtlede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.14"/> wæron: ⁊ hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.3"/> fule wurdon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.15"/> ⁊ hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.3"/> niten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.16"/>, hwa hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.3"/> on borh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.7"/> nime, gebringe man hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.8"/> on carcerne ⁊ man hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.3"/> don<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star2"/> út, swa hit her beforan cweden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.17"/> is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="154" ed="#liebermann"/>Be anfealdum ordale. And we cwædon be ðæm anfealdum ordale æt ðæm mannum ðe ðeofþe getyhtlod wæron: ⁊ hi fule wyrden ⁊ hí nyten, hwa hi on borh nime, gebringe hine mon on carcerne ⁊ hine man dó ut, swa her beforan gecweden is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="155" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.13"/> simplici ordalio. Diximus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.14-2"/> de simplici ordalio: Homo qui sepe fuerit accusatus et reus fiat (appareat) et nesciat, quis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.15-2"/> eum sumat in plegium, ponatur in carcere et educatur inde, sicut supra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.16-2"/> dictum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.17-2"/> est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-so-ot-from-swa-hit"><pb n="154" ed="#liebermann"/>Be anfealdum ordale. We cwædon be anfealdum ordale æt ðæm mannum þe oft getyhlod wæron: ⁊ hie fule wyrðen ⁊ hie nyten, hwa hi on borh nime, gebringe hine mon on carcerne ⁊ hine mon do út<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star-2"/>, swa hit her<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.oe.2"/> beforan gecweden is.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="130" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be anfealdum ordale.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="27" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.27"/> ⁊ we cwædon be ðam anfealdum ordale æt þam monnum þe oft betihtlede<ptr type="editorNote" n="28" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.28"/> wæron: ⁊ hy fule wurdon<ptr type="editorNote" n="29" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.29"/> ⁊ hy niten, hwa hy on borh nime, gebringe man hy<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.1"/> on carcerne ⁊ man hy<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.2"/> do<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.3"/> út, swa hit her beforan cweden<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.fn.4"/> is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="155" ed="#liebermann"/>Vom einfachen Ordal. Und wir bestimmten über das einfache<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.de.1"/> Ordal bei den Leuten, die oft (Diebstahls<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.de.2"/> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>) bezichtigt worden sind: [wenn] sie schuldig befunden wurden und niemanden wissen, wer sie in Bürgschaft nehme, so bringe man sie (ihn <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi>) ins Gefängniss und man lasse sie [nur] so<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_7.lnote.de.3"/> heraus, wie es hier zuvor bestimmt steht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the single ordeal. And we determined concerning the single ordeal for those people who have often been accused (of theft, Ld): [if] they were found guilty and know of no one who will take them into surety, let them (him, So Ld) be brought to prison and let them out [only] as is laid down here above.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="131" ed="#attenborough"/>And we have declared, with regard to the simple ordeal<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_7.attnote.n.1"/> for men who have often been accused of theft, and have been found guilty [thereby], and do not know anyone who will stand as surety for them, they shall be put in prison and they shall be liberated [only] on the conditions stated above.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="420" ed="#whitelock"/>And we have pronounced concerning the simple ordeal, with regard to those men who have often been accused, and were convicted, and know no one to stand surety for them; they are to be brought to prison, and they are<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_7.whinote.n.1"/> to be released as it is said here above.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="155"><ref target="clause:IIAs_6-1">II As 6.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IIAs_1-3">II As 1.3ff.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. 6, 1; 1, 3 ff.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 6.1 and 1.3 ff. H lacks the heading. The surviving burnt Ot resumes at ‘swa hit her beforan gecweden is’.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze Rubrik aus Ld So Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply the rubric from Ld So Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur hinter</hi> i</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">und</hi> do <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u and do on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> i <hi rend="italic">Rasur;</hi> e <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> o</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">after i an erasure; e altered to o</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">h <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">h on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> dó <hi rend="italic">aus Ld So Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read dó from Ld So Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> gecweden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to gecweden</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">conuicto <hi rend="italic">fügt zu M Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">conuicto added by M Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De si. o. di. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De si. o. di. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">predictum <hi rend="italic">T M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">predictum T M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">155</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">diximus <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">diximus R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">von hier an ist Ot erhalten; Unleserliches ergänze ich [in Klammern] aus So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from here on Ot is preserved; what is illegible I supply [in brackets] from So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">154</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Es handelt sich also um geringere Verbrechen als Herrenverrat, Kirchenerbrechung, Mord (<hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 4 ff.), von denen nur dreifach Ordal reinigte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">These are therefore lesser crimes than treachery to a lord, breaking into churches and murder (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> 4 ff.), from which only the threefold ordeal cleared a man</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ld's Abweichung ist laut Hss.-Stammbaums nicht archetyp, aber sinngemäss, nur vielleicht zu eng</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld’s variant is, according to the stemma of the MSS, not archetypal, but it agrees with the sense, only perhaps too narrowly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_7.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der doppelte Wechsel zum Sing. <hi rend="italic">hine,</hi> obwohl ungrammatisch, scheint mir archetyp. Nach der Strafe des Gefängnisses (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6 c ff.) muss 120 Schill. für sie bezahlt werden, oder sie bleiben Fiskalknechte wie in II Ew 6 bis zum Abverdienen jener Summe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The double change to the sing. <hi rend="italic">hine,</hi> although ungrammatical, seems to me archetypal. After the punishment of imprisonment (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6 c ff.) 120 shill. must be paid for them, or they remain slaves of the fisc, as in II Ew 6, until they have worked off that sum</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_7.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See note to Ine, cap. 37.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_7.attnote.fn.27" n="27" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope></bibl><label>ordale</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Ld, So.</seg></note>
